0. GOLDEN RULES FOR CURSOR (read first, apply to everything)
Pin to the exact versions in Section 2. Do NOT install "latest" of anything unless told. Version drift is the #1 cause of crashes for this project. When adding any package, use npx expo install <package> (NOT npm install) so Expo picks the version tested for this SDK.
Never generate deprecated code. Specifically: use Expo Router (not React Navigation manually), use expo-secure-store current API, use the @supabase/supabase-js v2 client, use function components with hooks only (no class components), use TypeScript everywhere.
Every async operation gets a try/catch and a user-visible fallback. No silent failures. No unhandled promise rejections. If a Supabase call fails, the user sees a friendly message and the app stays alive.
Never let the app crash to a white/blank screen. Wrap the app in an Error Boundary. Every screen must render something even if data is missing.
No secrets in the app code. The Supabase anon key is fine (it's public by design with RLS). Nothing else. No service-role keys, ever.
Explain like I don't code. When you finish a step, tell me in plain English what you did, what I need to do in the Supabase dashboard (if anything), and how I'd change it later. Keep code comments plentiful and beginner-friendly.
When unsure, ask me one clear question rather than guessing. A wrong assumption that compiles is worse than a question.
Build incrementally and keep it runnable. After each day's tasks in Section 9, the app must still start with npx expo start without errors. Never leave the project in a broken state between steps.
1. WHAT WE ARE BUILDING (Phase 1 scope)

Product name shown to users: **PRESCOPE** (folder on disk may still be LifeMate; Expo slug may still be LifeShield).

A mobile app that takes one user through: Sign up → symptom safety check → consent → a 9-section health & lifestyle questionnaire → an automatic list of recommended tests (generated by a rules engine, not AI) → a simple results screen. Everything saves to Supabase.

IN scope for Phase 1: auth, symptom triage + safe exit, sequential consent, the full questionnaire, the rules engine, a recommendations screen, basic profile/logout.

OUT of scope for Phase 1 (do not build, do not stub elaborate versions): AI chat, supplement store, payments, real lab-ordering APIs, push notifications, practitioner portal, B2B dashboard. We validate the core loop with real users first.

Positioning: a lifestyle awareness tool, not a diagnostic/medical app. Copy must never say it diagnoses, detects, or treats anything.

2. EXACT TECH STACK & VERSIONS (do not deviate)

Current stable as of this build (August 2026):

Thing	Version / Choice	Notes
Node.js	22.13.x or newer	Expo SDK 57 requires this minimum. Check with node --version before starting.
Expo SDK	57 (React Native 0.86, React 19.2.3)	Create with the command in Section 3.
Router	expo-router (comes with template)	File-based routing. Do not hand-roll navigation.
Language	TypeScript	Strict mode on.
Backend	Supabase — @supabase/supabase-js v2	Auth + Postgres + Row Level Security.
State	zustand (latest for RN)	Simple global state, no boilerplate.
Styling	nativewind v5 + tailwindcss	See Section 5 for the exact crash-proof setup — NativeWind misconfiguration is a known silent-failure trap.
Forms	react-hook-form + zod + @hookform/resolvers	Validation without crashes.
Secure storage	expo-secure-store	For the auth session.
Icons	@expo/vector-icons (bundled)	Don't add a separate icon library.

If any npx expo install reports a compatibility warning, STOP and show me the warning rather than forcing the install.

3. PROJECT CREATION (Cursor: run these, explain each)
bash
# 1. Confirm Node is 22.13+ first
node --version

# 2. Create the project with the current SDK and TypeScript + Router template
# (Historical folder name. The product users see is PRESCOPE.)
npx create-expo-app@latest LifeShield

# 3. Move into it
cd LifeShield

# 4. Verify it's on SDK 57
npx expo-doctor@latest

create-expo-app ships the current stable SDK (57) with expo-router and TypeScript already wired. Do not downgrade. If expo-doctor flags anything, show me before continuing.

4. INSTALL DEPENDENCIES (use expo install, not npm install)
bash
# Supabase + required polyfills for React Native
npx expo install @supabase/supabase-js @react-native-async-storage/async-storage react-native-url-polyfill

# Secure storage for the session
npx expo install expo-secure-store

# State management
npm install zustand

# Forms + validation
npm install react-hook-form zod @hookform/resolvers

# Styling (NativeWind v5 — see Section 5 for config, this order matters)
npm install nativewind
npx expo install react-native-reanimated react-native-safe-area-context
