After installing, run npx expo start --clear once to confirm a clean boot before writing any screens.

5. NATIVEWIND SETUP (crash-proofing — do this precisely)

NativeWind "installs fine but styles silently don't apply" is a well-known trap caused by wrong config paths or Metro cache. Follow this exactly:

Create tailwind.config.js at project root:
js
/** @type {import('tailwindcss').Config} */
module.exports = {
  content: ["./app/**/*.{js,jsx,ts,tsx}", "./components/**/*.{js,jsx,ts,tsx}"],
  presets: [require("nativewind/preset")],
  theme: {
    extend: {
      colors: {
        sage: "#A8C5A0",
        cream: "#FFF8F0",
        teal: "#1A535C",
        coral: "#FF6B6B",
        charcoal: "#2D3436",
      },
    },
  },
  plugins: [],
};
Create global.css at project root:
css
@tailwind base;
@tailwind components;
@tailwind utilities;
Import global.css at the very top of app/_layout.tsx.
Configure metro.config.js and babel.config.js per the NativeWind v5 docs for the installed version. After config, ALWAYS restart with npx expo start --clear (cache clear) — stale Metro cache is why styles "don't work" even when config is right.
Verification step (do not skip): before building real screens, put one <Text className="text-coral"> on screen and confirm it renders coral. If it doesn't, the problem is config/cache, not the code — fix it now, not later.
6. SUPABASE — BACKEND A NON-CODER CAN MANAGE
6.1 Why Supabase (so you understand what you own)

Supabase gives you a visual dashboard where you can see every user, every questionnaire answer, and every recommendation as simple spreadsheet-like tables — no code needed to read or edit data. You'll manage the backend almost entirely from the browser.

6.2 One-time setup (you do this in the browser, Cursor guides you)
Go to supabase.com → create a free project. Save the Project URL and anon public key (Settings → API).
Open the SQL Editor → paste the SQL in Section 6.4 → Run. This creates all tables and security rules in one go.
That's it. You now have a working backend.
6.3 Connecting the app

Create a .env file at project root (Cursor: also add .env to .gitignore):

EXPO_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=paste_your_project_url_here
EXPO_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=paste_your_anon_key_here

Cursor: create lib/supabase.ts using these env vars, with react-native-url-polyfill/auto imported at the top and AsyncStorage set as the auth storage, autoRefreshToken true, persistSession true. This is the standard crash-free RN Supabase setup — use the current documented v2 pattern.

6.4 Database schema (paste into Supabase SQL Editor)
sql
-- ========== PROFILES ==========
CREATE TABLE public.profiles (
  id UUID PRIMARY KEY REFERENCES auth.users(id) ON DELETE CASCADE,
  full_name TEXT,
  date_of_birth DATE,
  sex TEXT CHECK (sex IN ('male','female','other')),
  height_cm NUMERIC,
  weight_kg NUMERIC,
  bmi NUMERIC GENERATED ALWAYS AS (weight_kg / NULLIF((height_cm/100.0)^2,0)) STORED,
  waist_cm NUMERIC,
  hip_cm NUMERIC,
  ethnicity TEXT,
  country_of_origin TEXT,
  onboarding_completed BOOLEAN DEFAULT FALSE,
  created_at TIMESTAMPTZ DEFAULT NOW()
);
ALTER TABLE public.profiles ENABLE ROW LEVEL SECURITY;
CREATE POLICY "own_profile" ON public.profiles
  FOR ALL USING (auth.uid() = id) WITH CHECK (auth.uid() = id);

-- ========== TRIAGE ==========
CREATE TABLE public.triage_responses (
  id UUID PRIMARY KEY DEFAULT gen_random_uuid(),
  user_id UUID REFERENCES public.profiles(id) ON DELETE CASCADE,
  has_pain BOOLEAN NOT NULL,
  has_discomfort BOOLEAN NOT NULL,
  has_lump BOOLEAN NOT NULL,
  is_symptomatic BOOLEAN GENERATED ALWAYS AS (has_pain OR has_discomfort OR has_lump) STORED,
  triaged_at TIMESTAMPTZ DEFAULT NOW()
);
ALTER TABLE public.triage_responses ENABLE ROW LEVEL SECURITY;
CREATE POLICY "own_triage" ON public.triage_responses
  FOR ALL USING (auth.uid() = user_id) WITH CHECK (auth.uid() = user_id);

-- ========== CONSENT ==========
CREATE TABLE public.consent_records (
  id UUID PRIMARY KEY DEFAULT gen_random_uuid(),
  user_id UUID REFERENCES public.profiles(id) ON DELETE CASCADE,
  consent_type TEXT NOT NULL CHECK (consent_type IN ('terms_privacy','brca','ctc','snp')),
  consented BOOLEAN NOT NULL,
  consented_at TIMESTAMPTZ DEFAULT NOW()
);
ALTER TABLE public.consent_records ENABLE ROW LEVEL SECURITY;
CREATE POLICY "own_consent" ON public.consent_records
  FOR ALL USING (auth.uid() = user_id) WITH CHECK (auth.uid() = user_id);

-- ========== QUESTIONNAIRE ==========
CREATE TABLE public.questionnaire_responses (
  id UUID PRIMARY KEY DEFAULT gen_random_uuid(),
  user_id UUID REFERENCES public.profiles(id) ON DELETE CASCADE,
  section TEXT NOT NULL CHECK (section IN (
    'reproductive_menstrual','radiation_occupational','comorbidities',
    'family_history','personal_history','lifestyle','stress',
    'diet_environment','prior_screening'
  )),
  responses JSONB NOT NULL,
  completed_at TIMESTAMPTZ DEFAULT NOW(),
  UNIQUE (user_id, section)
);
ALTER TABLE public.questionnaire_responses ENABLE ROW LEVEL SECURITY;
CREATE POLICY "own_questionnaire" ON public.questionnaire_responses
  FOR ALL USING (auth.uid() = user_id) WITH CHECK (auth.uid() = user_id);

-- ========== TEST RECOMMENDATIONS ==========
CREATE TABLE public.test_orders (
  id UUID PRIMARY KEY DEFAULT gen_random_uuid(),
  user_id UUID REFERENCES public.profiles(id) ON DELETE CASCADE,
  test_tier INTEGER NOT NULL CHECK (test_tier IN (1,2,3,4)),
  test_name TEXT NOT NULL,
  trigger_reason TEXT,
  status TEXT DEFAULT 'recommended',
  created_at TIMESTAMPTZ DEFAULT NOW()
);
ALTER TABLE public.test_orders ENABLE ROW LEVEL SECURITY;
CREATE POLICY "own_tests" ON public.test_orders
  FOR ALL USING (auth.uid() = user_id) WITH CHECK (auth.uid() = user_id);

-- ========== AUTO-CREATE PROFILE ON SIGNUP ==========
-- So a profile row always exists the moment a user registers.
CREATE OR REPLACE FUNCTION public.handle_new_user()
RETURNS TRIGGER LANGUAGE plpgsql SECURITY DEFINER AS $$
BEGIN
  INSERT INTO public.profiles (id) VALUES (NEW.id);
  RETURN NEW;
END; $$;

CREATE TRIGGER on_auth_user_created
  AFTER INSERT ON auth.users
  FOR EACH ROW EXECUTE FUNCTION public.handle_new_user();

What this gives you: every table has Row Level Security so users can only ever see their own data (privacy by default), and a new profile row is created automatically on signup so the app never hits a "missing profile" crash.

6.5 How you'll manage it later (no code)
See users: Dashboard → Table Editor → profiles
Read someone's answers: Table Editor → questionnaire_responses → the responses column is readable JSON
Change a dropdown option, question, or threshold: those live in the app code (Sections 7 & 8) in clearly-marked config files — one-line edits, Cursor can do them in seconds
Change who can see what: Authentication → Policies (visual editor)
7. QUESTIONNAIRE — FULL FIELD DETAIL (from the source clinical document)

Cursor: build these as 9 sections. Put ALL option lists into lib/constants.ts so they can be edited in one place later. Each section saves one row to questionnaire_responses (section name + a JSON object of answers). Use react-hook-form + zod for every field so bad input can't crash a save.

Section 1 — Demographics & Anthropometrics → saves to profiles

Date of birth (date picker) → auto-calc age
Sex (radio: Male / Female / Other)
Height cm (number), Weight kg (number), BMI (auto, read-only)
Waist cm (number, "how to measure" tooltip), Hip cm (number, tooltip), Waist-to-hip ratio (auto, read-only)
Ethnicity (dropdown + "Other" free text), Country of origin (dropdown)

Section 2 — Reproductive & Menstrual History → reproductive_menstrual

Age at first period (number)
Contraceptive use (Yes/No) → if Yes: type (pill/IUD/implant/injection/patch/other), duration years
Amenorrhoea / missed periods (Yes/No) → if Yes: episodes count, cause (optional free text)
Menstrual regularity (Regular/Irregular), cycle length days, menopausal status (Pre/Peri/Post)
Pregnancies (number), live births (number), age at first birth (number, if births>0), breastfeeding (Yes/No → months)
→ SYMPTOM INTERRUPT immediately after (see Section 7A)

Section 3 — Radiation & Occupational Exposure → radiation_occupational

Radiation exposure (Yes/No) → if Yes: type (medical/occupational), body area, approx dates
Occupation (text)
Night-shift work (Yes currently / Yes in past / No) → if Yes: total years

Section 4 — Comorbidities & Chronic Infection → comorbidities

Gilbert syndrome / mildly raised bilirubin (Yes/No/Don't know)
Gallstones (Yes/No)
Obesity (Yes/No — cross-check with BMI)
Diabetes (Yes/No)
Thyroid disease (Yes/No) → if Yes: type
Active autoimmune thyroid disease — Hashimoto's/Graves' (Yes/No) ← SAFETY GATE for the iodine rule, never omit
Chronic infection (multi-select checkboxes): Dental / Gut / Urinary / Chest-respiratory / Sinus / Skin / None

Section 5 — Family History → family_history

Breast cancer (Yes/No) → if Yes: repeatable [relationship][age at diagnosis]
Ovarian cancer (Yes/No → relationship)
Colon cancer (Yes/No → relationship)
Melanoma (Yes/No → relationship)
→ SYMPTOM INTERRUPT immediately after (see Section 7A)

Section 6 — Personal History → personal_history

Smoking (Current/Former/Never) → if Current/Former: cigs per day + years (for pack-years)
Vaping (Yes/No → frequency)
Alcohol (units per week, number, "what's a unit?" tooltip)
Recreational drugs (Yes/No → optional type)
Caffeine (None / 1-2 / 3-4 / 5+ cups per day)

Section 7 — Lifestyle → lifestyle

Sleep hours per night (number), quality (Good/Fair/Poor)
Relationships / social support (Strong/Moderate/Limited)
Exercise: type (multi-select), frequency (Daily/3-5x/1-2x/Rarely/Never), duration (<15/15-30/30-60/60+ min)
Water intake (<1L/1-2L/2-3L/3L+)
Place of work (text), commute to city (Yes/No → method+duration)
Pollutant exposure (Yes/No/Unsure), vehicle exhaust exposure (Yes/No)

Section 8 — Stress module → stress (exact wording from source document)

Self-rated stress (Low/Medium/High)
"Do you tend to view stress as harmful, or as something you can learn and grow from?" (Harmful / Growth opportunity / Mixed)
"When under stress, do you reach out to other people, pets, or your community for support and connection?" (Usually/Sometimes/Rarely/Never)
Inline note: framing guides the stress-coping plan, not blame or causation

Section 9 — Diet & Environmental/Cosmetic Exposure → diet_environment

Canned/tinned food frequency (Daily/Weekly/Monthly/Rarely/Never)
Packaged/processed food frequency (same scale)
Takeaway frequency (same scale)
Microwave use (Regularly/Sometimes/Never)
Plastic containers/wrap (Regularly/Sometimes/Never)
Suncream (Daily/When sunny/Rarely/Never)
Nail varnish/gels (Regularly/Occasionally/Never)
Other cosmetics (multi-select: Foundation/Moisturiser/Deodorant/Perfume/Hair products/None)
Dietary iodine sources (multi-select: Iodised salt/Seafood/Seaweed/Dairy/None) ← feeds iodine rule

Section 10 — Prior Screening → prior_screening

Previous mammogram (Yes/No) → if Yes: repeatable [date][finding: Normal/Abnormal/Awaiting]
On submit → run rules engine → write test_orders → go to Results
Section 7A — The Symptom Interrupt (reusable safety component)

A component shown after Section 2 and after Section 5:

"Have you recently noticed any nipple discharge, breast skin changes, or a new lump?"

Yes → immediately navigate to Pathway B exit, lock the questionnaire, do not allow return
No → continue This exists because new symptoms mid-questionnaire must override everything and route to urgent care. Never skip or reorder these.
8. THE RULES ENGINE (pure logic, NO AI — this is the app's brain)

Build lib/rules-engine.ts and lib/clinical-thresholds.ts. This is deterministic IF-THEN logic — do NOT call any AI model for these decisions. It must be testable and auditable.

8.1 lib/clinical-thresholds.ts — single source of truth for every number
ts
// ⚠️ ASSUMED = placeholder, confirm with clinician later
// ✅ CONFIRMED = from source document or clinician
export const THRESHOLDS = {
  fastingInsulin_elevated: 8,      // ✅ CONFIRMED (source doc)
  bmi_obesityThreshold: 30,        // ✅ CONFIRMED (source doc)
  tsh_subclinicalHypo: 4.5,        // ✅ CONFIRMED (clinician)
  liverEnzyme_altAstElevated: 40,  // ⚠️ ASSUMED
};
export const HIGH_RISK_OCCUPATIONS = [
  "construction", "dentistry", "welding",  // ✅ CONFIRMED (source doc)
  "manufacturing", "mining",               // ⚠️ ASSUMED extensions
];

Keeping every clinical number here means future changes are one-line edits in one file — safe for a non-coder to hand to Cursor.

8.2 lib/rules-engine.ts — Tier 4 test triggers (from source document's algorithmic rules)

Implement these functions. In Phase 1 there are no lab results yet, so any input coming from bloods/SNP is passed as null; those rules return "recommended once baseline results are available" instead of firing — which is correct and honest for this stage.

shouldOrderDUTCH — fires if: SNP variant in CYP1A1/CYP1B1/COMT/MTHFR (null in Phase 1) OR (abnormal cortisol AND medium/high stress — cortisol null in Phase 1, so this leans on the stress answer) OR current/recent HRT or contraceptive use (from questionnaire — WORKS in Phase 1).
shouldOrderStoolAnalysis — fires if: estrogen-dominant history or impaired COMT (SNP null) OR chronic gut infection / gallstones (questionnaire — WORKS) OR fasting insulin > threshold (null) OR BMI > 30 (questionnaire — WORKS).
shouldOrderUrinaryIodine — SAFETY HARD-STOP first: if thyroid antibodies positive (null in Phase 1) OR active autoimmune thyroid disease = Yes (questionnaire — WORKS) → BLOCK and return reason. Otherwise fires on low dietary iodine (questionnaire — WORKS) or subclinical hypo (labs null). Uses THRESHOLDS.tsh_subclinicalHypo.
shouldOrderHeavyMetals — fires if: occupation in HIGH_RISK_OCCUPATIONS or pollutant/exhaust exposure (questionnaire — WORKS) OR unexplained liver enzymes + Gilbert's + exposure (labs null, partially works).

Each function returns { recommended: boolean, reason: string }. The submit handler in Section 10's screen loops these, and for every recommended: true, inserts a row into test_orders with the tier, test name, and reason. Also always add the Tier 3 baseline panel (routine bloods, thyroid + antibodies, B12/folate/ferritin, fasting insulin, salivary cortisol) as recommended for every Pathway A user, per the source document.

When you build this, put a clear comment block at the top: "This file contains clinical decision logic. Every rule maps to the source protocol. Do not use AI/LLM here. Changing a rule = changing one function below."

