Day 1 — Project + deps + NativeWind verification (Sections 3-5). Build lib/supabase.ts, the Error Boundary, and the root _layout.tsx with an auth gate. Deliverable: app boots, shows a placeholder home if logged in, login screen if not.

Day 2 — Auth: register, login, session persistence via secure store + AsyncStorage. Confirm a profile row auto-creates on signup (the trigger from 6.4). Build Splash + Welcome + Disclaimer + Terms consent.

Day 3 — Symptom triage (three toggles: pain/discomfort/lump) + Pathway B exit. Wire the branch: any symptom = go to Pathway B, cannot return. Test this hard — it's the safety core.

Day 4 — Sequential consent screens (BRCA → CTC → SNP), each saving to consent_records. Build the Questionnaire Hub with a 10-section progress tracker that reads completion from Supabase.

Day 5 — Questionnaire sections 1-5 (Demographics, Reproductive, Radiation, Comorbidities, Family History) with the symptom interrupt after Reproductive and after Family History. Save-and-resume via questionnaire_store + Supabase.

Day 6 — Questionnaire sections 6-10 (Personal, Lifestyle, Stress, Diet/Environment, Prior Screening). Build clinical-thresholds.ts and rules-engine.ts in full. On final submit, run the engine and write test_orders.

Day 7 — Results screen (recommendations grouped by tier, each with its reason). Profile/logout screen. Full end-to-end test: sign up → triage → consent → all 10 sections → see recommendations. Fix every warning expo-doctor reports. Confirm no red screens, no unhandled rejections.

After each day, run npx expo start --clear and confirm a clean boot before moving on.

10. ERROR-PROOFING CHECKLIST (Cursor: satisfy all of these)
 Root _layout.tsx wraps everything in an Error Boundary that shows a friendly "Something went wrong, tap to retry" screen instead of crashing.
 Every Supabase call is in try/catch; on error, show a toast/inline message, never a blank screen.
 Every screen handles the loading state (spinner) and the empty/missing-data state (friendly text) — no screen assumes data exists.
 All form inputs validated with zod before any save; invalid input shows a message, never crashes.
 No any types left unhandled; no unused imports; no console errors on boot.
 .env is git-ignored; no keys other than the Supabase URL + anon key anywhere.
 Numbers from inputs are parsed safely (guard against NaN before saving to numeric columns).
 The symptom-interrupt and triage routing cannot be bypassed by back-button navigation.
 npx expo-doctor@latest passes with no errors.
 App has been cold-started at least once on a real phone via Expo Go without crashing.
11. HOW TO CHANGE THINGS LATER (so you're never stuck)
Reword a question / add a dropdown option: edit lib/constants.ts (all option lists live there). Ask Cursor: "add option X to the Y list in constants."
Change a clinical number: edit lib/clinical-thresholds.ts, one line.
Change a rule: edit the one function in lib/rules-engine.ts.
See/adjust user data: Supabase dashboard → Table Editor (no code).
Change colours/branding: edit the theme colors in tailwind.config.js.
Add a new question section later: add it to the section CHECK list in the DB, add a screen file, add it to the hub tracker. Ask Cursor and it's a 15-minute change.

Keep this file (.cursorrules) in the project. Any future Cursor session should read it first so the app stays consistent and crash-free.

